 "schema": "pcc.claim/v1",
 "scope": "research/base-point-independence-20261108/README.md",
 "statement": "In any additive commutative group with n \u2022 P = 0 and c * c' \u2261 1 (mod n), (k * c') \u2022 (c \u2022 P) = k \u2022 P and k' \u2022 (c \u2022 P) = Q implies (k' * c) \u2022 P = Q (logarithms transfer between base points of the subgroup); with P of exact order n the map k \u21a6 k \u2022 P is injective on residues below n; the points (k + i*d) \u2022 P have constant difference d \u2022 P and satisfy Q_i = Q_0 + i \u2022 (d \u2022 P); and pairwise sums of {1..B} \u2022 P lie in {2..2B} \u2022 P."
}
